<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Hebrew translation of the device health report (Issue #24).

    The folder qualifier is "iw" for the same reason as strings.xml: Android
    resolves resource folders against java.util.Locale#getLanguage(), which
    still reports the legacy Hebrew code.

    Latin runs inside a Hebrew sentence (Android, Device Owner) are wrapped in
    U+2066 LEFT-TO-RIGHT ISOLATE / U+2069 POP DIRECTIONAL ISOLATE so the bidi
    algorithm cannot drag the surrounding punctuation to the wrong side.
    Runtime values — timestamps, versions, origins, package names — are
    isolated in code instead; see ui/UiLogic.kt.

    Keys and format placeholders are kept in parity with
    res/values/device_health_strings.xml by DeviceHealthStringsParityTest.java.
-->
